{"id":"Q1041","iso2":"SN","iso3":"SEN","name":"Senegal","wiki":"Senegal","description":"country on the coast of West Africa","flag":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fd/Flag_of_Senegal.svg/330px-Flag_of_Senegal.svg.png","capital":"Dakar","capitalCoord":[14.672555555,-17.432],"inception":"1960-01-01","government":["presidential system"],"legislature":["National Assembly"],"continent":["Africa"],"website":"https://www.sec.gouv.sn/","offices":[{"id":"Q19116034","role":"hog","title":"President of Senegal"},{"id":"Q19116034","role":"hos","title":"President of Senegal"}],"currentHog":"Q124382437","currentHos":"Q124382437","terms":[{"office":"Q19116034","roles":["hog","hos"],"person":"Q154545","start":"1960-09-06","end":"1980-12-31"},{"office":"Q19116034","roles":["hog","hos"],"person":"Q219728","start":"1981-01-01","end":"2000-04-01"},{"office":"Q19116034","roles":["hog","hos"],"person":"Q106963","start":"2000-04-01","end":"2012-04-02"},{"office":"Q19116034","roles":["hog","hos"],"person":"Q57438","start":"2012-04-02","end":"2024-04-02"},{"office":"Q19116034","roles":["hog","hos"],"person":"Q124382437","start":"2024-04-02","end":null}],"people":{"Q154545":{"id":"Q154545","name":"Léopold Sédar Senghor","desc":"first president of Senegal, poet, and cultural theorist (1906–2001)","img":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a8/L%C3%A9opold_S%C3%A9dar_Senghor.jpg/330px-L%C3%A9opold_S%C3%A9dar_Senghor.jpg","gender":"M","born":"1906-10-09","died":"2001-12-20","birthplace":"Joal-Fadiouth","parties":["French Section of the Workers' International","Socialist Party of Senegal"],"education":["Faculty of Arts of Paris","École Normale Supérieure","Lycée Louis-le-Grand"],"occupations":["politician","poet","writer","French resistance fighter"],"wiki":"Léopold Sédar Senghor"},"Q219728":{"id":"Q219728","name":"Abdou Diouf","desc":"Senegalese President","img":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b3/Abdou_Diouf.jpg/330px-Abdou_Diouf.jpg","gender":"M","born":"1935-09-07","died":null,"birthplace":"Nguer Malal","parties":["Socialist Party of Senegal"],"education":["University of Paris 1 Pantheon-Sorbonne","Université Cheikh Anta Diop"],"occupations":["politician","lawyer","head of government"],"wiki":"Abdou Diouf"},"Q106963":{"id":"Q106963","name":"Abdoulaye Wade","desc":"3rd President of Senegal","img":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d2/Abdoulaye_Wade_2011.jpg/330px-Abdoulaye_Wade_2011.jpg","gender":"M","born":"1926-05-29","died":null,"birthplace":"Kébémer","parties":["Senegalese Democratic Party"],"education":["Lycée Condorcet","Marie and Louis Pasteur University"],"occupations":["politician","lawyer","university teacher","jurist"],"wiki":"Abdoulaye Wade"},"Q57438":{"id":"Q57438","name":"Macky Sall","desc":"4th President of Senegal, formerly Prime Minister","img":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7c/Macky_Sall_with_Obamas_2014_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Macky_Sall_with_Obamas_2014_%28cropped%29.jpg","gender":"M","born":"1961-12-11","died":null,"birthplace":"Fatick","parties":["Senegalese Democratic Party","Alliance for the Republic"],"education":["Université Cheikh Anta Diop","IFP School"],"occupations":["politician","engineer"],"wiki":"Macky Sall"},"Q124382437":{"id":"Q124382437","name":"Bassirou Diomaye Faye","desc":"President of Senegal since 2024","img":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2f/Bassirou_Diomaye_Faye_9_juillet_2025_Washington_DC_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Bassirou_Diomaye_Faye_9_juillet_2025_Washington_DC_%28cropped%29.jpg","gender":"M","born":"1980-03-25","died":null,"birthplace":"N’Diaganiao","parties":["African Patriots of Senegal for Work, Ethics and Fraternity"],"education":["Université Cheikh Anta Diop","National School of Administration of Senegal"],"occupations":["Inspecteur général des finances","politician"],"wiki":"Bassirou Diomaye Faye"}},"summary":"Senegal, officially the Republic of Senegal, is the westernmost country of mainland West Africa, situated along the Atlantic Ocean coast. It borders Mauritania to the north, Mali to the east, Guinea to the southeast and Guinea-Bissau to the southwest. Senegal nearly surrounds the Gambia, a country occupying a narrow strip of land along the banks of the Gambia River, which separates Senegal's southern region of Casamance from the rest of the country. It also shares a maritime border with Cape Verde. The capital and largest city of Senegal is Dakar.\nSenegal is the westernmost country in the mainland of the Old World and Afro-Eurasia. It owes its name to the Senegal River, which borders it to the north and east. The climate is typically Sahelian, with a rainy season. Senegal covers a land area of almost 197,000 square kilometres (76,000 sq mi) and has a population of around 18 million. The state is a semi-presidential republic; since its foundation in 1960, it has been recognized as one of the most stable countries on the African continent. On the 2024 V-Dem Democracy Indices, Senegal is ranked 68th in electoral democracy worldwide and 10th in electoral democracy in Africa.\nThe state was formed as part of the independence of French West Africa from French colonial rule. Because of this history, French is the official language, but it is understood by only a small minority of the population. Over 30 languages are spoken; Wolof is the most widely spoken, with 80% of the population speaking it as a first or second language, acting as the lingua franca alongside French. Arabic and Pulaar are popular among certain communities. Like other African nations, the country includes a wide mix of ethnic and linguistic communities, with the largest being the Wolof, Fula, and Serer people. Senegalese people are predominantly Muslim.\nAs a developing nation, Senegal is classified as a heavily indebted poor country, with a relatively low ranking on the Human Development Index (169th out of 193). Most of the population lives on the coast and works in agriculture or other food industries; other major industries include mining, tourism, and services. The historic lack of natural resources has directed efforts towards increasing literacy and educational attainment. Senegal is a member state of the African Union, the United Nations, the Economic Community of West African States (ECOWAS), Organisation internationale de la Francophonie, the Organisation of Islamic Cooperation, and the Community of Sahel–Saharan States.","history":"The history of Senegal is commonly divided into a number of periods, encompassing the prehistoric era, the precolonial period, colonialism, and the contemporary era.","historyTitle":"History of Senegal","curated":null,"indicators":{"gdpPerCapita":[[1960,300.425],[1961,308.166],[1962,307.093],[1963,308.63],[1964,317.85],[1965,314.318],[1966,314.534],[1967,305.22],[1968,311.196],[1969,287.253],[1970,290.486],[1971,291.088],[1972,341.835],[1973,381.439],[1974,417.408],[1975,547.378],[1976,540.594],[1977,540.127],[1978,589.134],[1979,716.281],[1980,771.534],[1981,682.972],[1982,651.937],[1983,564.369],[1984,536.232],[1985,571.417],[1986,783.941],[1987,916.095],[1988,880.488],[1989,848.556],[1990,957.314],[1991,913.4],[1992,951.205],[1993,877.529],[1994,583.783],[1995,714.994],[1996,723.47],[1997,650.776],[1998,684.588],[1999,677.516],[2000,603.233],[2001,637.214],[2002,669.43],[2003,817.888],[2004,918.102],[2005,979.846],[2006,1017.2],[2007,1188.94],[2008,1398.79],[2009,1308.69],[2010,1275.88],[2011,1374.68],[2012,1326.84],[2013,1379.83],[2014,1398.89],[2015,1218.01],[2016,1266.44],[2017,1354.77],[2018,1452.56],[2019,1431.18],[2020,1461.09],[2021,1598.11],[2022,1574.03],[2023,1698.03],[2024,1738.73],[2025,1954.71]],"population":[[1960,3340910],[1961,3436380],[1962,3534690],[1963,3635880],[1964,3740540],[1965,3849790],[1966,3964300],[1967,4083870],[1968,4207590],[1969,4334970],[1970,4466330],[1971,4601860],[1972,4741630],[1973,4885180],[1974,5029440],[1975,5170810],[1976,5308560],[1977,5